{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 121, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When the cell already has convs on the internal path, swapping the residual skip on edge 3 for another conv removes a useful shortcut, whereas in conv-free cells it adds the only learnable op (exp 72,76 vs 71,73,74)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "If edge 5 is a parameter-free pool, adding a conv on edge 4 provides much-needed learnable capacity on the output, giving large gains (exp 61-65 vs 20-23)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual skip on edge 3 helps deep conv cells but is harmful in parameter-free skip/pool cells where it replaces or dilutes the only signal (exp 7-10 vs 11-13)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, removing edge 0 cuts all input flow into intermediate nodes, collapsing paths through edges 4/5 (exp 18,19 vs 14-17)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 3 (or nothing) feeding the output, causing severe degradation (exp 99 vs 98)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, edge 3 is a critical output path, so removing it is catastrophic (exp 39,40 vs 38,41)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with a 1x1 loses receptive field, while replacing skip/pool/none with 1x1 adds capacity (exp 54 vs 55-57)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 carries a 3x3 conv, edge 4 transports that learned node-1 feature to the output, so removing it hurts more than when node 1 holds a cheap op (exp 77,81 vs 78-80)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the edge-3 residual, a smoothing pool on edge 5 stabilizes an all-conv cell, while with a residual present swapping a conv for pooling just loses capacity (exp 97 vs 32,35)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells, a skip on edge 3 bypasses the remaining processing or replaces the only conv, severely hurting accuracy (exp 12,13 vs 7-10,86)."}], "tok": 17689, "bad": 1, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect",